From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A Canonical <canonical@ls1046a-build>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 03:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: P0 CC-automation — auto-build F-171 fe_group at engage

The F-171 CONT_LOOKUP group wrap (fe_group) is currently debugfs-only:
the board procedure must hand-build it (`echo build > fe_group`) and
re-engage with the returned group_ad offset before the experimental
group dispatch can be exercised. Automate the build so the manual step
disappears:

- __fman_pcd_fe_arm_engage() pre-builds the group (wrapping the FE_ENTER
  root AD, miss -> miss_fqid, all-wildcard match row) whenever the root
  AD exists. Production dispatch is UNCHANGED: RCCB still targets the
  vendor node at gro; the group is prebuilt state only, consumed when
  the debugfs engage verb is given its group_ad offset.
- __fman_pcd_fe_arm_disengage() frees the shared group once the last
  armed port disengages (fe_group is per-PCD, not per-port).

Both call sites precede the definitions (engaged ~3708, disengage
~3917 vs definitions at 4637/4714), so forward declarations are
added after the includes.

Throwaway experiment branch (P0.8). Guarded by the existing
-EEXIST/-ENOENT returns of fman_pcd_fe_group_build(); any build failure
degrades to the current behavior with a warning.

Patch-Name: 0197-fman-pcd-fe-group-autobuild.patch
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -47,8 +47,14 @@
 #include "fman.h"
 #include "fman_muram.h"
 #include "fman_port.h"
 #include "fman_keygen_internal.h"
 
+/* Forward declarations (0197): both defined later (0173 fe_group
+ * section); engage/disengage call them before their definitions. */
+static int fman_pcd_fe_group_build(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u32 miss_fqid,
+				   const u8 *key, const u8 *mask);
+static void fman_pcd_fe_group_free(struct fman_pcd *pcd);
+
 /* F-210(v6-enable-gate): IPv6 FE offload master switch. 2026-08-21:
  * DEFAULT ON. IPv6 now uses the SAME dual-lane match-all scheme + per-
  * port 46-byte table as IPv4 (F-224/F-225); the old v6-only machinery
@@ -3708,14 +3714,31 @@ static int __fman_pcd_fe_arm_engage(struct fman_pcd *pcd,
 	/* C2 readback gate (F-008): validate MURAM before KG arm.
 	 * Catches silent-write defects before frames hit silicon. */
 	{		int _verify_err = fman_pcd_fe_verify_internal(pcd, (u8)port_id);
 		if (_verify_err) {
 			pr_err("fman_pcd: arm_engage 0x%02x ABORTED — verify failed\n",
 			       (u8)port_id);
 			return _verify_err;
 		}	}
 
+	/* P0 CC-automation (0197): pre-build the F-171 CONT_LOOKUP group
+	 * wrap (fe_group) when the FE_ENTER root AD exists, so the
+	 * experimental group dispatch is available without the manual
+	 * debugfs build step. Production dispatch is unchanged: RCCB
+	 * still targets the vendor node at gro; the group is prebuilt
+	 * state only, consumed by the debugfs engage verb.
+	 * -EEXIST = already built (e.g. second port's engage).
+	 */
+	if (pcd->fe_root_ad_off && !pcd->fe_group_off) {
+		int _grp_err = fman_pcd_fe_group_build(pcd,
+					      miss_fqid ? miss_fqid : 0x200,
+					      NULL, NULL);
+		if (_grp_err && _grp_err != -EEXIST)
+			pr_warn("fman_pcd: fe_group prebuild failed (%d)\n",
+				_grp_err);
+	}
+
 		err = fman_pcd_kg_port_arm_fe(pcd, (u8)port_id,
 				      (u32)fe_enter_off, &saved_engine, ekfc);
 	if (err) {
 		/*
 		 * F-125: release the scaffold we just built. Returning with
@@ -3917,8 +3940,14 @@ static int __fman_pcd_fe_arm_disengage(struct fman_pcd *pcd,
 	}
 	fsleep(5000);
 	fman_pcd_fe_port_del(pcd, (u8)port_id);
 	/* F-139: scaffold now freed in fe_port_del */
 
+	/* P0 CC-automation (0197): release the shared F-171 group wrap
+	 * once the last armed port disengages (fe_group is per-PCD,
+	 * not per-port). */
+	if (bitmap_empty(pcd->fe_port_armed, 32))
+		fman_pcd_fe_group_free(pcd);
+
 	pr_info("fman_pcd fe_arm: port 0x%02x DISENGAGED\n", port_id);
 	return 0;
 }
